\caption{The Thompson automaton for \code{a(b|c)*}. Solid arrows are epsilon
transitions; dashed arrows are the loop back edges installed by the \code{*}
quantifier. The \code{x} and \code{y} labels mark the two successor slots of
the split states: the quantifier split sends its \code{x} branch back into
