Reading the figure from left to right: the program starts at the epsilon
state 0, which hops to the literal \code{a}. The literal hops to the
quantifier split 7, whose \code{y} branch ends the match and whose \code{x}
branch enters the alternation split 6. That split has one branch for each
alternative, and each alternative ends by hopping back to state 7, closing
the loop.

